1
00:00:05,579 --> 00:00:09,121
The sign is drawn, machined and simulated. What does the machine get?

2
00:00:09,121 --> 00:00:18,576
Program shows the woodWOP macros this part makes: two drillings, a pocket, a contour.

3
00:00:18,576 --> 00:00:23,561
Each one opens in woodWOP as an editable macro, not a long list of points.

4
00:00:23,561 --> 00:00:31,212
Custom-part output is off by default, so for now this preview is for checking only.

5
00:00:31,212 --> 00:00:38,904
Now put the sign in the Goldberg job. Open the job’s Custom parts tab.

6
00:00:38,904 --> 00:00:43,702
Add from the part library: one click on the Goldberg sign.

7
00:00:43,702 --> 00:00:52,719
It now nests with the cabinet parts. Here it lands on an MDF sheet of its own.

8
00:00:52,719 --> 00:01:01,626
Output: the check notes that only its cut-out would be cut while custom-part output is off.

9
00:01:01,626 --> 00:01:04,828
Switch it on under Machine & tools when you are ready, and simulate in woodWOP first.
